#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "8559e2bf-8b48-5e26-81c6-0db03d93645a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5451" :question/problem "What linear transformation is represented by the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/assets/6191f617d2c2e89e07c1cc349a5926874f11ea78d046185ce990e566225a7c79.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j} \\}$ of the Euclidean plane $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as depicted below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nWe can find the images of $\\{ \\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j} \\}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/assets/b93bb91dae85a3e3b40a8d0ade3d4f420064aaa6926431fa7f664c977bb8fd59.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents the reflection across the $x$-axis."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/id #uuid "ef17b637-7c4d-5515-99b7-13b1290244f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-5452" :question/problem "A linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ represents a dilation. Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/assets/bd6574ee05b60919de656a889f8532e5a512b381eae63f7a65f251a7afe72738.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/assets/be73c2a933a6fb99eaa389774a618848bdadd9cafdf0fcd2f6af126b49b87707.png) what is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}) = \\dfrac{1}{4}\\mathbf{v},$ we conclude that the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k = \\dfrac{1}{4}.$\n\nRemember that the matrix representing a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/assets/4866597a50fbdb530e9275c77f2ca926c932c7cc334635bd05191aaddd510d75.png)\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/assets/962b9458714f9b7f6b17fe2259e140dfabba443d8ecb5b9e2328172ab3f8a1a2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac2c45bf-ce21-5500-b6b8-4a67992f33e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329922} {:answer/id #uuid "2b4fdafe-a381-526f-9e3f-bc8756696836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329923} {:answer/id #uuid "4e8d9aac-82fe-5314-8dcd-f155fdaf2e04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329924} {:answer/id #uuid "5b975215-a5a1-5e6a-9a97-1a27ac5cafd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{12}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329925} {:answer/id #uuid "c4c055da-2be3-5f07-876f-79488482b53a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b4fdafe-a381-526f-9e3f-bc8756696836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329923} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8eaee76-14e4-5f04-9c0d-3dafd350d084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0591c45f-50ff-5065-b712-d7946fc4e140" :question/math-academy-id "q-12043" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=12.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4073c80c-940d-5e0e-be1f-922bd077ff76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4073c80c-940d-5e0e-be1f-922bd077ff76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329929} :answer-field/id #uuid "d610250f-2f12-579c-89be-e21e9e32036e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329928} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd6c76b-b561-51cc-9dfb-620d5004e16f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cd6c76b-b561-51cc-9dfb-620d5004e16f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329931} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c4e4682-5605-576d-9b9e-4f93301557e6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "573d11fe-f168-5694-9e5d-e084b7a21207" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "573d11fe-f168-5694-9e5d-e084b7a21207" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329933} :answer-field/id #uuid "09699a05-2c9b-5c63-9279-e63a126234b0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329932} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec3195d7-179d-5b5c-b3b0-66c6a37ef464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec3195d7-179d-5b5c-b3b0-66c6a37ef464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329935} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f65501b-4364-5cc8-8739-8ece7041cac6" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef035e6f-20ac-50ef-9479-1744ff9ac796" :question/math-academy-id "q-275741" :question/problem "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix $T$ of $T?$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=3v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=3.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "addc8e22-aaac-5014-909f-83097d927c11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "addc8e22-aaac-5014-909f-83097d927c11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329938} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d962377-d3df-5162-9e8a-b71395e2942f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329937} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "269b9d27-1c06-56a6-9fcc-9ff9c15caf03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "269b9d27-1c06-56a6-9fcc-9ff9c15caf03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329940} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf756b2e-3365-5727-abba-7cbd18109a5a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a093622-61a6-5d3e-a5bb-7d67deba468f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a093622-61a6-5d3e-a5bb-7d67deba468f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329942} :answer-field/id #uuid "af63a823-7d3e-555a-8146-d93719c6cd83" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329941} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cacb67f2-c979-5343-bc7e-e9b2a5230818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cacb67f2-c979-5343-bc7e-e9b2a5230818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329944} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dcbe692-7b89-5060-816f-7a3d053c7d12" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8dd5e696-aae8-5123-8741-ba6c2486aad1" :question/math-academy-id "q-328216" :question/problem "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix $T$ of $T?$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=2v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=2.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2326f32d-c93e-5caa-93cf-3b4d871487ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2326f32d-c93e-5caa-93cf-3b4d871487ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329947} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a118ad-6986-5db6-828d-a8c87e40152f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329946} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21ad0e15-7770-50ee-b1f7-079b492ceb6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21ad0e15-7770-50ee-b1f7-079b492ceb6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329949} :answer-field/id #uuid "483ed58b-8dd5-54a1-8750-a3cdb1cac29c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329948} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fad3a23-78a6-51c4-a58b-2333a736bb9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fad3a23-78a6-51c4-a58b-2333a736bb9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329951} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d4aadb6-c7b5-5872-bbde-34807337f54e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329950} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "901e3945-b616-58fd-8109-35770c0b765a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "901e3945-b616-58fd-8109-35770c0b765a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329953} :answer-field/id #uuid "08feb553-cce5-5bb9-9009-5aa815a0fd3f" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4c87835-c9a6-5cbd-ac5a-906e93e64385" :question/math-academy-id "q-328234" :question/problem "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix $T$ of $T?$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{7}{4}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db586b66-6d18-5494-a52e-33e8b3dbdddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329956} {:answer/id #uuid "a4620a0d-b9bf-51e7-845d-b9e04b0d5e9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 \\\\ 9 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329957} {:answer/id #uuid "0655f82e-fa0a-5084-ae08-81af20bc668b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329958} {:answer/id #uuid "31b69651-4955-5ced-b538-93801be15f01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329959} {:answer/id #uuid "76b4fbb5-4dd8-551a-af39-1b134ee55171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db586b66-6d18-5494-a52e-33e8b3dbdddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329956} :answer-field/id #uuid "b63f5e75-b270-591d-9a68-fe9a98042bd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "954d7834-0128-5286-a434-cb6d547ab390" :question/math-academy-id "q-78247" :question/problem "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}72 \\\\ -40\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}72 \\\\ -40\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =8\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =8v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=8v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=8.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Matrix of a Dilation Given a Vector and its Image"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2df0dc52-11a2-5bc1-ac6b-ecfd669f2b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329963} {:answer/id #uuid "57750657-ae2a-541a-8cbd-4feabc8d76e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329964} {:answer/id #uuid "8bfedff4-0355-5b91-b95c-50340f09a459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329965} {:answer/id #uuid "adef0d61-23f2-51ea-ad40-21e962d34517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329966} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd3f596-3b12-5df1-87e0-6df036d5ba71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecd3f596-3b12-5df1-87e0-6df036d5ba71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329967} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ca949ac-becc-5490-a220-59ad3d6dc317" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba67f8b5-b4aa-5dbc-8d3f-1501ac2571d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-78295" :question/problem "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}-54 \\\\ 81\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-54 \\\\ 81\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{9}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{9}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "892c68cb-26fd-5950-89aa-95af200ef566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086749} {:answer/id #uuid "dc390f5f-54e3-5dbe-a1d8-9c5cebeebd6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086750} {:answer/id #uuid "472454e6-6141-5a63-9f61-ce5b4c149f65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086751} {:answer/id #uuid "4dcc7404-55cb-5603-9405-272b2d821e08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086752} {:answer/id #uuid "77a41bcf-dcc5-5714-b8fd-ca53ea1a599a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc390f5f-54e3-5dbe-a1d8-9c5cebeebd6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086750} :answer-field/id #uuid "767f5b44-4e93-5075-ae32-e55eb00505c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086748}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cad47c40-27a1-5f31-8c6f-6a66b9bee47d" :question/math-academy-id "q-78299" :question/problem "Which of the following represents a reflection across the $y$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14052682/assets/4993d8586a84e4a40a54edddd8011cd3d516264bfffc7e3c33d27a10edf1e7d7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06a16ffb-8eb5-5341-a162-599742a0b2ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=17$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329970} {:answer/id #uuid "a521248a-22ad-5707-91c8-6c41faeb5af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $17$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329971} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f8dab9-274c-5180-a5fc-7bc9f2a6838c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{17}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329972} {:answer/id #uuid "63482a43-98c9-5f2d-82df-193474b58d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $x$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329973} {:answer/id #uuid "d24c1bda-5422-5419-9ccb-e89a9b284dd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a521248a-22ad-5707-91c8-6c41faeb5af0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $17$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329971} :answer-field/id #uuid "14352b75-10fa-5698-8338-de34f8148a00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85f3d75b-9319-5b51-9847-8f5fa211a35d" :question/math-academy-id "q-78337" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}17 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 17\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=17.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $17.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf99414e-f1cf-528f-adbb-407cf6e82c4c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Linear Transformation Represented by a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bee11fb-76ab-5911-9495-00fbe496dee8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329977} {:answer/id #uuid "378fa887-59e4-5290-afbe-872ecba22c71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection across the $y$-axis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329978} {:answer/id #uuid "b51f3b23-7258-5d41-a1a9-9c014da73d45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329979} {:answer/id #uuid "ed990d8e-c9a0-50fa-bce2-1b9e91c6ce28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $x=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329980} {:answer/id #uuid "95947fcb-2db1-5f47-b7a5-b39d165e7448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Reflection in the line $y=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b51f3b23-7258-5d41-a1a9-9c014da73d45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Dilation with scale factor $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329979} :answer-field/id #uuid "424df4a1-8609-5ff4-9089-20bc2c6a11de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-fi