 17592186329984} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5466a01-7dfc-5f4c-89ce-cdba385fd402" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0816025c-46e7-58ec-8914-573277dafb44" :question/math-academy-id "q-8088" :question/problem "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=\\frac{1}{4}.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $\\frac{1}{4}.$"}]}
